Hughshine","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODQ2MDc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine","user_view_type":"public"},"commit_id":"5cf59b1df2a769b96e5849197a3bb9ca0b04815a","commit_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hughshine/triton/commits/5cf59b1df2a769b96e5849197a3bb9ca0b04815a","created_at":"2026-06-29T06:14:07Z","event":"referenced","id":27314601199,"node_id":"REFE_lADOAWaHXs8AAAABHACBPs8AAAAGXBO87w","performed_via_github_app":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/events/27314601199"},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32846078?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Hughshine","id":32846078,"login":"Hughshine","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODQ2MDc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hughshine","user_view_type":"public"},"created_at":"2026-06-29T07:00:03Z","event":"cross-referenced","source":{"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"# New contributor declaration\r\n- [x] I am not making a trivial change, such as fixing a typo in a comment.\r\n\r\n- [x] I have written a PR description following these\r\n  [rules](https://cbea.ms/git-commit/#why-not-how).\r\n\r\n- [x] I have run `pre-commit run --from-ref origin/main --to-ref HEAD`.\r\n\r\n- Select one of the following.\r\n  - [x] I have added tests.\r\n    - `/python/test/unit` for end-to-end tests\r\n\r\n- Select one of the following.\r\n  - [x] I have not added any `lit` tests.\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nThe FNUZ fp8 formats (`e4m3fnuz`, `e5m2fnuz`) encode their single NaN as the byte\r\n`0x80` — the slot IEEE-style formats use for `-0`, which FNUZ repurposes (these\r\nformats have no `-0` and no `Inf`). On AMD targets without native FNUZ fp8\r\nconversion (everything except CDNA3), the upcast is done in software, and the\r\nsoftware decoders turn `0x80` into a finite signed value instead of NaN —\r\nsilently corrupting any downstream NaN propagation/masking.\r\n\r\n## Root cause (three software decoders)\r\n\r\n- `Fp8E4M3fnuzToFp16OneValue`: a NaN guard mapping `0x80 → 0x7E00` is present, but\r\n  the denorm/zero LUT (`vAbs == 0 → 0x0000`) and the trailing `a = b.or_(a, sign)`\r\n  run *after* it, so for `0x80` the LUT overwrites the NaN and the sign re-apply\r\n  yields `0x8000` (fp16 `-0.0`).\r\n- `Fp8E5M2fnuzToFp16OneValue`: no `0x80` case at all — `exp == 0` takes the\r\n  `e_is_zero` branch and produces `sign | (m >> 1) = 0x8000`.\r\n- `Fp8E4M3fnuzToBf16SW`: its own bit-trick decoder turns `0x80` into bf16 `-0.0`;\r\n  there is no NaN guard.\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\n\r\n- `e4m3fnuz → f16`: move the `0x80 → 0x7E00` NaN guard to be the **last** write,\r\n  after the sign re-apply, so neither the LUT nor the sign-or can clobber it.\r\n- `e5m2fnuz → f16`: add the same `0x80 → 0x7E00` guard before the final bitcast.\r\n- `e4m3fnuz → bf16`: add a per-lane `0x80 → 0x7FC0` (bf16 NaN) guard on the two\r\n  unpacked output lanes.\r\n\r\nThe two remaining fnuz upcasts route through the above and are fixed transitively:\r\n`e5m2fnuz → bf16` calls `Fp8E5M2fnuzToFp16SW`, and both `→ f32` go\r\nfp8 → fp16 → fp32. So all six `{e4m3fnuz, e5m2fnuz} × {f16, bf16, f32}` upcasts\r\nnow preserve NaN.\r\n\r\nThe OCP (non-fnuz) `e4m3fn` / `e5m2` decoders are intentionally unchanged:\r\n`e4m3fn` has a signed zero, so its `0x80 → -0.0` is correct.\r\n\r\n## Test\r\n\r\n`test_typeconvert_upcast_fnuz_nan` in `python/test/unit/language/test_conversions.py`\r\nconverts a buffer of the NaN byte `0x80` for `float8e4b8`/`float8e5b16` →\r\n`float16`/`bfloat16`/`float32` and asserts the result is NaN. This is the one\r\ninput the exhaustive upcast test masks out (it replaces `0x80` with `0` before\r\nconverting), so it was previously untested. It skips on non-HIP, RDNA3 and CDNA2\r\n(where fnuz upcast is unsupported) and runs on the non-CDNA3 software-decode path\r\nwhere the bug lives.\r\n\r\nFixes #10745","closed_at":"2026-07-12T02:09:20Z","comments":2,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/10747/comments","created_at":"2026-06-29T07:00:02Z","draft":false,"events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/10747/events","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/10747","id":4765786408,"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/10747/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAWaHXs7rqDSg","number":10747,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pull_request":{"diff_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/10747.diff","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/10747","merged_at":"2026-07-12T02:09:20Z","patch_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/10747.patch","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/pulls/10747"},"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket"